### Prior art

Raven's Stellar repository index surfaced [SocketFi's Soroban smart account](https://github.com/Socket-Fi/socketfi-smart-account)
and [Crossmint's Stellar smart account](https://github.com/Crossmint/stellar-smart-account)
on 2026-10-25. A source scan of SocketFi (scanned 2026-09-16, Soroban SDK
`=25.3.1`) found signer/auth-context handling and session policies. This is
adjacent prior art, not evidence that its policies implement this POC's exact
contract-and-function allowlist. Neither repository has been audited as part
of this setup.

## Initial acceptance criteria

- A valid signature from the configured `G...` signer authorizes an allowlisted
  contract/function pair.
- A call to an unlisted function or contract is rejected.
- An allowed outer call cannot smuggle an unlisted nested invocation.
- Invalid signatures, unknown authorization contexts, and an empty policy fail
  closed.
- Tests cover both permitted and rejected paths before testnet deployment.
